kernora-base (1.4) UNRELEASED; urgency=high

  * Withdraw the automatic RTL8852CE power-saving override after a report of
    packet loss and lag spikes in CS2 after the update. Causality is unproven.
  * Keep the workaround as an inactive example for explicit opt-in use.
    Upgrade removes the vendor policy without rewriting saved profiles or
    administrator overrides. Restart to restore normal device defaults.

 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0700

kernora-base (1.3) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Disable NetworkManager Wi-Fi power saving by default for RTL8852CE only
    to avoid a possible source of intermittent disconnects. Preserve explicit
    connection preferences and other adapters' power policies.
  * Reload configuration without restarting NetworkManager on upgrade.
    The default takes effect on the next connection or reboot.

 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:30:00 -0700

kernora-base (1.2) UNRELEASED; urgency=high

  * Repair the root directory ownership on upgrade from affected live ISOs.
    A non-root owner prevented systemd-tmpfiles and the login screen from
    starting correctly after installation.

 -- Kernora Developers <developers@kernora.invalid>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 13:40:00 -0700

